WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.760
Integrating OT monitoring with a security operations center combines established alert

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.500
workflows with industrial visibility.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.000
The SOC can provide continuous triage, correlation, case management, and escalation,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.065
while OT specialists provide the asset, protocol, process,

00:00:14.065 --> 00:00:16.680
and safety context needed for sound decisions.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.000
Forward selected OT events to the SIEM rather than every available record without purpose.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.060
Preserve useful fields such as asset identity, zone, function, protocol, command category,

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.500
user, remote session, maintenance state, and criticality.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.270
Time synchronization and consistent naming are essential for correlation.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.000
Detection content should link enterprise and OT pathways.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.055
A compromised identity, VPN session, jump-host event, firewall connection,

00:00:39.055 --> 00:00:42.500
and unusual controller communication may form one investigation.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.400
The SOC needs contacts and runbooks that explain who can validate each stage and which

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.760
actions require operational approval.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.985
Monitoring can update asset inventory by revealing new devices, changed communication,

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.995
or dormant systems returning to service.

00:00:54.995 --> 00:00:59.055
Vulnerability management can use observed reachability and software clues to improve

00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:00.260
prioritization.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.055
Architecture teams can compare actual traffic with approved conduits and segmentation

00:01:04.055 --> 00:01:04.460
policy.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.770
Governance should define data ownership, retention, access, alert service levels,

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.536
escalation, monitoring health, and coverage gaps.

00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:15.835
Reports should communicate meaningful risk: unsupported sensors, unmonitored sites,

00:01:15.835 --> 00:01:19.995
repeated unauthorized access, baseline drift, unresolved high-consequence alerts,

00:01:19.995 --> 00:01:21.770
and time to coordinated response.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.890
Integration does not mean removing OT authority or treating industrial alerts exactly like

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:26.975
office endpoints.

00:01:26.975 --> 00:01:29.200
It creates a shared operating model.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.770
Security operations contribute scale and consistency;

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.225
engineering and operations contribute process knowledge and safe response.

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:39.380
Together they turn telemetry into decisions that protect both the network and the physical

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:39.980
mission.
